;
; How Gleaner files one row of a dataset in MYRA (gleaner_rules.h GR4): its
; index in the file (0 .. 999), its label's class and its source, each an
; index into the dataset's own table (0 .. 63), its date as YYYYMMDD and
; whether it holds personal data (1) or not (0). Gleaner asks whether the
; numbers fit before it keeps them.
^ZXGLEAN(row:i3) = label:i2! ^ source:i2! ^ date:i8! ^ pii:i1!
